{"type": "pair", "at": "2026-11-27T02:04:15+00:00", "step": "omissions-20261127T020141Z", "issue": "whu-lean-orch-t1-q1-01d", "kind": "omission", "seed": 197649960427000, "ruling_id": "e5be9e366cfd7b26", "prompt_sha256": "bcae380e4e2b9bf580f406b62337b15840bfbeaad845f8b9da48634b5e10d6d0", "inputs_sha256": "ea28ae8695c558911226a5b93711d709f22d194341f7befe263cebf74c2d1538", "first": {"ruling": "add", "text": "Compared with digital messages that were not targeted to the individual, the review reports that targeted client communication via mobile devices (TCCMD) \"may reduce attendance for vaccinations, but the CI encompasses both benefit and harm (RR 0.63, 95% CI 0.33 to 1.20; low‐certainty evidence)\" [3]."}, "second": {"ruling": "add", "text": "Compared with digital non-targeted communication, the review found that targeted client communication via mobile devices \"may reduce attendance for vaccinations, but the CI encompasses both benefit and harm (RR 0.63, 95% CI 0.33 to 1.20; low‐certainty evidence)\" [3]."}, "usable": true, "agree_decision": true, "agree": false, "usage": {"input": 4616, "output": 941, "usd": 0.037284, "seconds": 9.0}, "applied": false}
{"type": "pair", "at": "2026-11-27T02:04:20+00:00", "step": "omissions-20261127T020141Z", "issue": "whu-lean-orch-t1-q1-01d", "kind": "omission", "seed": 197649960427000, "ruling_id": "7b1494b9790346e4", "prompt_sha256": "bcae380e4e2b9bf580f406b62337b15840bfbeaad845f8b9da48634b5e10d6d0", "inputs_sha256": "c5c3c07c5f91ab87267d4b4cce1d01cbfd8baa19ea3d3e0695317e3b720d30ce", "first": {"ruling": "not_material", "text": null}, "second": {"ruling": "not_material", "text": null}, "usable": true, "agree_decision": true, "agree": true, "usage": {"input": 4701, "output": 518, "usd": 0.029164, "seconds": 4.6}, "applied": false}
{"type": "pair", "at": "2026-11-27T02:04:30+00:00", "step": "omissions-20261127T020141Z", "issue": "whu-lean-orch-t1-q1-01d", "kind": "omission", "seed": 197649960427000, "ruling_id": "796cb3a320db05a5", "prompt_sha256": "bcae380e4e2b9bf580f406b62337b15840bfbeaad845f8b9da48634b5e10d6d0", "inputs_sha256": "e20cfd15fe4fa36bd751a739fffe17787911e7fa00bc8b81e0fb753ed1e00c41", "first": {"ruling": "add", "text": "Breaking down that comparison with digital non-targeted communication by type of service, one trial among men who have sex with men in Peru provided what the authors call \"moderate‐certainty evidence (downgraded once due to risk of bias) that TCC via mobile devices may have a large effect on increasing attendance for STI/HIV testing (RR 2.62, 95% CI 1.52 to 4.53; N = 498; 12 weeks follow‐up)\" [4]."}, "second": {"ruling": "add", "text": "Within the pooled comparison of targeted client communication via mobile devices with digital non-targeted communication, one trial among men who have sex with men in Peru provided moderate-certainty evidence (downgraded once due to risk of bias) that the intervention \"may have a large effect on increasing attendance for STI/HIV testing (RR 2.62, 95% CI 1.52 to 4.53; N = 498; 12 weeks follow-up)\" [4]."}, "usable": true, "agree_decision": true, "agree": false, "usage": {"input": 4880, "output": 1096, "usd": 0.04144, "seconds": 9.6}, "applied": false}
